  "changes": [
    "Independent v6 package and launchers; legacy, v4 and v5 frozen.",
    "Bundled validated 1850--2036 planet reference with separate interpolated proposal and exact authority interfaces.",
    "Batched exact visit refinement, deterministic per-planet workers, structured telemetry, and a controlled v5/v6 benchmark.",
    "Conservative two-anchor constellation recruitment tests all compatible one-to-one overrides and can recover a third or later Gaia-associated planet after a common-epoch refit, with explicit JSON/CSV audit fields.",
    "Closed centred full-horizon footprints provide a provisional image-centre zenith when extinction is not identifiable; boundary circle residuals, complete azimuth coverage and fitted-camera 90-degree rays reject ellipses, crops and round vignettes; strong photometric solutions retain authority and the rejected trial remains auditable."
  ],
